Rule 2 (x2 must have the same number of dimensions as x1)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (sizes along the reduction dimension must match, supporting negative dim)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: int} |= (v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, v_3) = shape(v_2, v_3)) ∨ (v_3 < 0 ∧ shape(v_1, v_3 + ndim(v_1)) = shape(v_2, v_3 + ndim(v_1)))
>>
Rule 4 (x1 and x2 must be broadcastable on all non-reduction dimensions)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: int} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if v_3 ≥ 0 then (if i = v_3 then true else (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)) else (if i = v_3 + ndim(v_1) then true else (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 5 (inputs must have floating-point dtypes)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 6 (eps must be positive)
{v_4: float} |= v_4 > 0
